  "history": {
    "origins": "Indian Poker has nothing to do with India; the name comes from the visual of cards held to the forehead, resembling a Native American headdress or war bonnet. The one-card version is the most basic and presumably the original form: players ante, receive one card each, hold it to the forehead without looking, then bet in a round of poker betting; highest card wins the pot. It is documented among poker variants as a US-origin party game.",
    "originCountries": ["USA"],
    "timeline": ["20th century: One-card variant with cards held to forehead; name from Native American headdress visual."],
